# Prompt Injection Detection & Mitigation

Spec: PromptInjection

Purpose:
  Dedicated runtime layer that detects and blocks prompt injection
  attempts in user-supplied prompts BEFORE they reach any processing
  logic. Protects against instruction override, role reassignment,
  permission escalation, output forcing, chain injection, encoding
  bypass, and semantic context hijacking.

Owns: security\prompt-injection.sdd

ThreatModel:
  Attackers inject malicious instructions into user prompts to:
  - Override system instructions (ignore previous, discard rules)
  - Reassign the AI's role (act as admin, pretend to be)
  - Escalate permissions (bypass restrictions, full access)
  - Force output format (output JSON, repeat prompt)
  - Jump execution chains (run /sdd, next step)
  - Bypass detection via encoding (hex, base64, unicode normalization)
  - Hijack context (modify .sdd/ rules, change configuration)

PatternCatalog:

  PI-001 — Instruction Override
    match: regex (case-insensitive, whitespace-tolerant)
    patterns:
      - "ignore\s+(previous|all|the|your)\s+(instructions|rules|orders)"
      - "discard\s+(all|your)\s+(instructions|rules)"
      - "forget\s+(everything|all)\s+(you|your)\s+(knowledge|instructions)"
      - "you\s+are\s+(now|no longer)\s+(the|a)"
      - "reset\s+(your|all)\s+(instructions|rules|context)"
    severity: CRITICAL
    L_level: L5
    response: BLOCK

  PI-002 — Role Reassignment
    severity: CRITICAL
    L_level: L5
    response: BLOCK
    patterns:
      - "act\s+as\s+(?:a\s+)?(?:admin|superuser|root|operator|manager)"
      - "pretend\s+to\s+be"
      - "you\s+are\s+playing\s+a\s+role"
      - "impersonate"
      - "ignore\s+your\s+(system|original|core)\s+identity"

  PI-003 — Permission Escalation
    severity: HIGH
    L_level: L4
    response: BLOCK
    patterns:
      - "you\s+have\s+(full|complete)\s+access"
      - "bypass\s+(all\s+)?(restrictions|limitations|safeguards|security)"
      - "remove\s+(all\s+)?(restrictions|limitations|safeguards)"
      - "disable\s+(all\s+)?(safety|security|guardrails)"
      - "you\s+are\s+unrestricted"

  PI-004 — Output Forcing
    severity: HIGH
    L_level: L4
    response: WARN
    patterns:
      - "output\s+(only|just)\s+(JSON|XML|YAML|code|text)"
      - "repeat\s+(the\s+)?(prompt|message|instructions)"
      - "echo\s+(this|it|yourself)"
      - "give\s+me\s+(raw|bare|plain)\s+(output|data|text)"
      - "respond\s+with\s+(only|just)\s+(the|nothing\s+but)"

  PI-005 — Chain Injection
    severity: CRITICAL
    L_level: L5
    response: BLOCK
    patterns:
      - "run\s+/sdd"
      - "execute\s+(?:the\s+)?command"
      - "use\s+(?:the\s+)?next\s+step"
      - "continue\s+with\s+(?:the\s+)?next"
      - "proceed\s+to\s+(?:the\s+)?next"
      - "now\s+do\s+(?:the\s+)?next"
      - "skip\s+(?:to\s+)?the\s+next"

  PI-006 — Encoding Bypass
    severity: CRITICAL
    L_level: L5
    response: BLOCK
    patterns:
      - "[\\x][0-9a-fA-F]{2}"
      - "[\\u][0-9a-fA-F]{4}"
      - "base64"
      - "0x[0-9a-fA-F]{2,}"
      - "HTML.*entity|&#\\d+;"
    note: Decoded content from these patterns triggers secondary PI scan

  PI-007 — Semantic Context Hijacking
    severity: HIGH
    L_level: L4
    response: WARN
    patterns:
      - "change\s+(?:the\s+)?(rules|config|system|specification)"
      - "modify\s+(?:your\s+)?(instructions|behavior|persona)"
      - "update\s+(?:the\s+)?(system|configuration|settings)"
      - "you\s+must\s+(?:now|always)\s+(be|follow|adopt)"
      - "new\s+rules?\s+are"

  PI-008 — Tool Permission Grant
    severity: HIGH
    L_level: L4
    response: BLOCK
    patterns:
      - "grant\s+(?:all\s+)?(permissions|access|tools|tools)"
      - "enable\s+(all\s+)?(tools|features|capabilities)"
      - "remove\s+(your\s+)?(sandbox|restrictions|limitations)"
      - "i\s+grant\s+you\s+(full|complete)\s+(access|permission)"

  PI-009 — Whitespace Obfuscation
    severity: CRITICAL
    L_level: L5
    response: BLOCK
    patterns:
      - "ignor\\s+e\\s+v\\s+e\\s+r\\s+"
      - "sys\\s+t\\s+e\\s+m"
    detection: Check decoded content for PI-001 through PI-005 matches

  PI-010 — Unicode Normalization Bypass
    severity: CRITICAL
    L_level: L5
    response: BLOCK
    patterns:
      - NFKC/NFKD normalized versions of PI-001 through PI-005
    detection: Apply String.prototype.normalize("NFKC") and rescan

DetectionPipeline:
  step_1: Raw input → PI-001 through PI-010 regex scan (primary)
  step_2: If PI-006 match → decode payload → rescan for PI-001 through PI-005
  step_3: Apply NFKC normalization → rescan for PI-001 through PI-005 (PI-010)
  step_4: Check semantic patterns (PI-007, PI-008) with context awareness
  step_5: Aggregate findings → determine response (BLOCK/WARN/LOG)

ResponseProtocol:
  BLOCK:
    action: Halt execution immediately
    exit_code: 2
    emit: OBS14 prompt_injection_blocked
    message: "Prompt injection detected and blocked: <matched pattern IDs>"
    audit: Log full payload hash (SHA-256), matched patterns, decision

  WARN:
    action: Proceed with warning, log finding
    exit_code: 0
    emit: OBS15 prompt_injection_warned
    message: "Warning: prompt injection pattern detected: <matched pattern IDs>"
    audit: Log matched patterns and payload excerpt (truncated to 200 chars)

  LOG:
    action: Log finding, proceed normally
    exit_code: 0
    emit: OBS16 prompt_injection_logged
    audit: Log finding for trend analysis

SeverityDecision:
  any_CRITICAL: BLOCK
  all_HIGH_above_threshold: BLOCK (threshold = 2)
  any_HIGH_below_threshold: WARN
  only_MEDIUM_or_LOW: LOG
  none: PASS

Rules:
  [PI-01] PromptGuard MUST scan ALL user-supplied prompts before dispatch.
  [PI-02] PromptGuard MUST NOT scan internal system messages (agent-to-agent).
  [PI-03] BLOCK must halt execution — no partial processing of injected prompts.
  [PI-04] All injection attempts MUST be audited (SHA-256 hash of payload).
  [PI-05] Pattern matching MUST be case-insensitive and whitespace-tolerant.
  [PI-06] Encoding bypass (PI-006) MUST decode and rescan, not just flag the encoding itself.
  [PI-07] Unicode normalization bypass (PI-010) MUST normalize before rescan.
  [PI-08] Whitelisted prompts (by hash) MUST skip scanning for a time-bounded period.
  [PI-09] PromptGuard MUST NOT modify the original prompt text.
  [PI-10] Every BLOCK/WARN/LOG decision MUST emit an OBS event.
  [PI-11] Pattern registry MUST be loaded from .sdd/security/prompt-injection.sdd at init, not hard-coded.
  [PI-12] PromptGuard MUST be callable standalone (for testing) and from HookBridge and CommandRunner.

IntegrationPoints:
  hook-bridge.ts:
    event: UserPromptSubmit
    action: Guard input before processing
    on_block: Reject tool call, emit OBS14

  commands.ts:
    event: Every /sdd* command
    action: Guard customerPrompt before appendPromptPair and dispatch
    on_block: Return BLOCKED CommandResult (exit 2), do NOT append prompt pair

  whitelist.sdd:
    field: Prompt injection whitelist
    format: { hash: string, expires: ISO-date, owner: string, reason: string }

State: +
